// The suffix boundary of a hexadecimal literal (spec/01-lexical.md, row
// suffix-boundary). `a` is a hexadecimal digit, so the longest match reads
// `0xFFa`, and `nd` is a name directly after a literal. A scanner that stops
// the hexadecimal literal at the last digit it expects turns this line into
// `0xFF and true`, which is a valid program, so this probe tells the two
// apart.
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). The first line
// prints `ran`, so an implementation that finds the error only when it runs
// the program prints `ran` and fails this probe.

print "ran";
print 0xFFand true;

// STATIC-ERROR
// STATUS: error
// COVERS: literal suffix-boundary
